            <ArticleTitle>[Use of strontium-89 in the analgesic treatment of cancer patients with bone metastases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>11-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The aim of this article was to review the available literature regarding to the use of strontium-89 in the palliation of osteoblastic bone pain. The data of many researchers showed that approximately 80% of patients with pain from osteoblastic lesions resulting from prostate or breast cancer experience significant pain relief by administration of strontium-89, with only mild levels of hematotoxicity. The duration of pain relief in some cases exceeded 3-6 months. Indications for administration of strontium-89, effectiveness and duration of the treatment, side effects are reviewed in this article.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
